From 527277e5fcf22cb628e8acdd1b0bd9d57bbb0fe2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cary Palmer <24235924+professorpalmer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 03:08:45 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] recurrent: replay rollback (LLAMA_RS_REPLAY=1): one
 recurrent-state plane instead of one per draft token

The GDN kernel runs each sequence's pending tokens (the inputs of its last P = n_rs_seq tokens, kept in p_l with a
valid count) before the batch, skipping the rejected ones, writes the state P tokens before the end (the commit point)
and the inputs of the last P tokens (ggml_gated_delta_net_replay). The chunked MMA prefill keeps the chunk boundaries
of the snapshot form (K = P + 1), so the results are the same bytes. Slot files: s_trans 2 (S plane + pending rows +
the rejected count). qwen35 with raw GDN gates, CUDA, one sequence per context; off by default.
